      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{59b80cbbd1662e660835c7c5|full_name}: This bug is in the current build 772 and has been around for awhile. Here is a test world that contains a chair that moves through a trigger collider looking for either \"player local\" or \"player\" layers. It will display when either event happens. Walking through it normally works. Sitting and then clicking the collider to move the chair does not trigger the event.\nwrld_c18fb7ee-0b68-4892-8b4f-6a323c93efc5",
